---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { formatLong, lastUpdated } from '../data/record';
---
<PageLayout
  title="About"
  heading="An open record of AI risk"
  description="How SafeAI.watch selects and reads its sources: what each entry records, how evidence is attributed, and the limits of the record."
  intro="SafeAI.watch brings together public research, reported incidents, warnings, and policy responses. Each entry keeps its source and the limits of its evidence in view."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <section id="method" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
      <h2 id="method-heading">How entries are read</h2>
      <p>
        Start with what happened and who reported it. Identify what the available evidence supports,
        then record the questions that remain unresolved. Publication dates describe when the linked
        source appeared.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
      <h2 id="sources-heading">Evidence and attribution</h2>
      <p>
        Company reports describe the company's findings. Preprints may change before peer review.
        Essays and interviews present arguments and forecasts. Reporting offers an account that readers
        can compare with original material.
      </p>
      <p>
        Capabilities evaluated under controlled conditions, warnings about future harm, and observed
        incidents are different categories. A serious warning can justify scrutiny while its probability
        remains uncertain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
      <h2 id="scope-heading">Scope of the record</h2>
      <p>
        The record is a selection of sources published through{' '}
        <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{formatLong(lastUpdated)}</time>, initially focused on AI and
        biological risk. It makes no claim to cover every development or to monitor events in real time.
      </p>
      <p>
        The featured GZERO World interview is linked editorial coverage. It is not an endorsement of this
        project. Illustrations are conceptual artwork and contain no measured results.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="further" aria-labelledby="further-heading">
      <h2 id="further-heading">Reading further</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/latest">Browse the source archive</a> or <a href="/timeline">follow the timeline</a>.
        Source links let readers examine the original context, revisions, and later developments.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="typefaces" aria-labelledby="typefaces-heading">
      <h2 id="typefaces-heading">Typefaces</h2>
      <p>
        The site is set in Geist and Geist Mono by Vercel and Newsreader by Production Type. All three
        are served from this site under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence texts: <a href="/licenses/OFL-Geist.txt">Geist</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/licenses/OFL-Geist-Mono.txt">Geist Mono</a>, <a href="/licenses/OFL-Newsreader.txt">Newsreader</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
